  "note": "benchmarks/perf/frame_times.cjs on an Apple M4 (10 CPUs, 16 GB), one run per size, under heavy system-wide swapping (the swap field). Datasets: lumencell synth --n-cells N (2,000 genes, bifurcation, realistic), prepared with lumencell prepare (100k: 204 s, 2.8 GB peak RSS; 500k: 2,148 s, 7.5 GB), root from lumencell roots, each launch running paga_dpt. 1M was not tried: 500k took 36 min to prepare and swap was nearly full. 500k_at_1x is a one-off diagnostic, the same script with deviceScaleFactor 1, to test whether pixel count is the limit: it is not, the numbers match 500k at 2x. An earlier one-off probe (not kept) counted vm_stat swap-ins per scenario at 500k: about 3,000 per second at rest, where every frame was on time, and about 3,500 per second during auto-rotate, so paging does not explain the slow frames either. main_ms_per_frame stays at 2 ms or less at 500k, so the slow frames are not the main thread: the limit is on the GPU side.",
